<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Edmund Ironside</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 990–1016</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Edmund II of England</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Edmund Ironside was king of the English for seven months in 1016, the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aethelred-the-unready">Æthelred the Unready</a>. He resisted Cnut's invasion vigorously, earning his nickname, but was defeated at the Battle of Assandun in October 1016. By the agreement that followed he kept <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wessex">Wessex</a> while Cnut took the lands north of the Thames, but Edmund died on 30 November 1016 and Cnut became king of all <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/edmund-ironside.jpg" alt="Edmund Ironside" width="320" height="293" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Edmund_Ironside_-_MS_Royal_14_B_VI.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
